  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "A second advance for Domdolus Tolus",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-12-2002-arc-2-three-teams-break-into-gold"
      ],
      "text": "Domdolus Tolus climbs to eighth at 65.14 after adding 13.47 points in the morning comparison window. It had already reached 51.67 on October 12; this is a separate improvement. The score event lifted it from thirteenth to eighth, while the midnight-baseline comparison records a climb from twelfth. That distinction matters in a moving field."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Csaky lands in gold, then the field moves",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-13-0203-arc-2-richard-csaky-enters-gold"
      ],
      "text": "Richard Csaky’s recorded overnight score event raised his mark from 30.97 to 58.33 and took him from 658th to ninth. Later advances leave him eleventh at the morning close, still comfortably inside the fifteen provisional gold places. Majkel1337 rises to tenth at 62.08, gaining 9.58 points overnight; Dawid Kopiczko holds seventh at 66.25 after adding 3.19. ARC Raiders is ninth at 64.58, with a recorded overnight score event from 62.08. Its full midnight comparison is unavailable, so that event should not be read as a certified net daily gain."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Yesterday’s gold entrants face a higher line",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-12-2158-arc-2-kajetan-schweighofer-enters-gold",
        "wire-2026-10-12-2358-arc-2-arcward-intelligence-nears-gold",
        "wire-2026-10-12-2002-arc-2-three-teams-break-into-gold"
      ],
      "text": "The gold cutoff rises from 47.92 at the baseline to 48.33, now held by yuritosci in fifteenth. Kajetan Schweighofer is sixteenth at an unchanged 47.92, outside the band after entering it on October 12. ARCward Intelligence, whose 45.42 breakthrough was also observed on October 12, is now seventeenth. The overnight wire carried both developments forward; neither is a second fresh score increase. ARCward is 2.91 points below today’s line. These public bands are provisional."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Tufa keeps the top steady",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-dries-smit-identity-0",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs remains first at 88.06, with rabbithole second at 80.56 and Yi-Chia Chen third at 77.22. Their scores are unchanged in this issue’s window. Chen is only 0.14 above fourth-placed nvbanana. Dries Smit remains listed in Tufa’s separate ARC-2 roster. The commissioned citadel illustration portrays that leading position; its GPUs, five spiders and digital rabbits are editorial metaphor, not evidence of the team’s hardware or headcount."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The queue remains part of the contest",
      "sourceIds": [
        "discussion-arc-2-747515"
      ],
      "text": "Scored results do not mean every pending run has finished. In the public queue-update thread, Kaggle staff member Dustin says the accounting error was fixed and that current capacity supports roughly one submission every other day per team. That is dated operational context; it does not establish that every present delay is resolved. The field can still change as more results arrive."
    }
  ],
